{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>I am your father-in-law, etc., and your wife, etc.</b> The reason the verse changed their order here from the order it wrote in the preceding verse, where it placed the sons before the wife, is explained according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Mekhilta; Exodus Rabbah 27:2), who said: if you do not come out for her sake, etc. If so, the verse arranged them from bottom to top; therefore it placed the wife before the sons — for if he would not act for her sake, he would act for the sake of the sons. This is unlike when the verse informed us of their arrival in the wilderness and arranged them in the order of the more honored first, placing the sons first. And although there Jethro was placed before the sons, while here he is arranged before the wife — which would suggest he is beneath her in rank — Jethro spoke in humility and lowliness, but the Scripture honored him and placed him first because he is Moses' father-in-law, and one must honor him even for Moses' sake, as it is written (I Samuel 24:11): ״וְאָבִי רְאֵה גַּם רְאֵה״.\"" "<b>And her two sons with her.</b> The reason it says <b>with her</b> is to convey a fourth argument: if you will not act for her sake alone and not for the sake of her sons alone, combine the honor of both of them and come out.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:31.082632909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}